/*
 * Settings storage relocated for the Open Bootloader layout.
 *
 * The board devicetree puts the storage partition at 0xF8000, inside the
 * region the Nordic Open Bootloader occupies (roughly 0xE0000 to 0x100000).
 * OpenThread writes its network credentials there through the settings NVS
 * backend, so on a DFU image the partition moves onto the bootloader's
 * application-data area at 0xDD000-0xDFFFF (12 kB, three NVS sectors). The
 * bootloader never erases those pages during DFU and refuses any image that
 * reaches into them, so the credentials survive a firmware update and no
 * update can clobber them.
 *
 * Pairs with dfu.conf. The unit-address of the node keeps the name it was
 * given in the board devicetree; only the address in reg is authoritative.
 */

&storage_partition {
	reg = <0x000DD000 DT_SIZE_K(12)>;
};
